      "proposed_replacement": "Suppose a smooth map $F:W^p\\to N$ to a boundaryless manifold and its boundary restriction are transverse to a closed embedded submanifold $Z$ of codimension $c$. If $c\\le p$, then $F^{-1}(Z)$ is an embedded manifold with boundary of dimension $p-c$ (possibly empty), with boundary $(F|_{\\partial W})^{-1}(Z)$; it is neat when $p-c\\ge1$, and lies in the interior with empty boundary when $c=p$. If $c>p$, then $F^{-1}(Z)=\\varnothing$",
